# ==============================================================================
# MEDCHECK — .gitignore
#
# Rule for editing this file: ANCHOR EVERY DIRECTORY PATTERN.
#
# A bare `foo/` matches a directory named `foo` at *any* depth, including inside
# the source tree. That is how a copy-pasted Python-packaging block came to carry
# `lib/`, which silently excluded `frontend/src/lib/` -- the directory holding
# `api.ts`, the only module that talks to the backend. Four components import it,
# so `npm run build` failed on every fresh clone and in CI, while working
# perfectly on the machine where the file already existed on disk.
#
# So: plain-word directories get a leading `/` or a full path. Only patterns that
# genuinely recur at every level of a tree (`__pycache__/`, `node_modules/`) or
# that are dot-prefixed (and therefore cannot collide with a source directory)
# are left unanchored.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets & environment
#
# `.env.*` is deliberately broad. The previous list enumerated .local,
# .production, .development and .docker, which meant a `.env.staging` or
# `.env.test` would have been committed. Catch everything, then re-admit the
# checked-in templates.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
.envrc
secrets/
*.pem
*.key

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local databases (SQLite cache, plus its WAL-mode sidecar files)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
#
# The setuptools/wheel distribution block that used to live here has been
# removed: MEDCHECK is an application, not a published package, so `sdist/`,
# `wheels/`, `*.egg-info/`, `lib/` and friends can never be produced here. One of
# them was actively destroying the frontend (see the header).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
backend/venv/

# Tooling caches (dot-prefixed, safe to leave unanchored)
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytype/
.pyre/
.dmypy.json

# Coverage
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.cover
.tox/
.nox/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend
#
# `package-lock.json` is intentionally NOT ignored -- it is what makes `npm ci`
# in CI reproducible.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/dist-ssr/
frontend/coverage/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/.turbo/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/storybook-static/
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo

# npm/yarn/pnpm diagnostics
.npm
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment & container local state
#
# `frontend/vercel.json` is committed; `.vercel/` is the CLI's per-machine link
# to a project and must not be.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vercel/
docker-compose.override.yml

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs & audit trails
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
/logs/
backend/audit_logs/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor, tooling & OS cruft
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.zed/
*.iml
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.code-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db

# Merge/patch leftovers
*.orig
*.rej

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch space
#
# Archives are never source. Note that blanket document ignores (`*.pdf`,
# `*.docx`) are deliberately absent -- a clinical project has legitimate reasons
# to commit a reference label or a printed brief, and an extension-wide rule
# drops such a file silently.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tmp/
/temp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# AI / agent scratch output
prompts/
*.prompt
ai-generated/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal planning docs (PRD, architecture notes, design-system specs, phase
# roadmap). Excluded as working notes rather than shipped documentation -- the
# public-facing docs are README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and CHANGELOG_CLINICAL.md.
# Delete this line to start tracking them.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/docs/
